---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageFrame from '../components/PageFrame.astro';
import Masthead from '../components/Masthead.astro';
import WorkSection from '../components/WorkSection.astro';
import ActionRow from '../components/ActionRow.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/TextLink.astro';
import Dot from '../components/Dot.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import FactsList from '../components/FactsList.astro';
import CaseLead from '../components/CaseLead.astro';
import MetaLine from '../components/MetaLine.astro';
import PointsList from '../components/PointsList.astro';
const head = `<link rel="icon" href="data:," />`;
const afterFooter = ``;
---
<Base title={"Datomania - Gorka Molero Case Study"} description={"Case study for Datomania, a civic-data product around public-interest datasets, provenance modeling, Representantes records, API/export routes, and methodology."} page="datomania">
  <Fragment slot="head" set:html={head} />
  <PageFrame class="sheet">
    <Masthead />
    

      <CaseLead class="lead">
        <MetaLine class="meta eyebrow">Live · data product</MetaLine>
        <h2 class="case-title">Datomania</h2>
        <p class="intro">A public-data product around information that should be easier to access: provenance modeling, Representantes records, API/export routes, and methodology.</p>
        <MetaLine class="meta chips">Public on gorkamolero <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> 1,257 records <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> API / export surfaces</MetaLine>
      </CaseLead>

      <main>
      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>Problem</h2>
        <p>Public-interest data often technically exists, but is hard to browse, verify, export, or use in software. A useful civic-data product needs more than a table: it needs provenance, methodology, API access, and a product surface that makes the data understandable.</p>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>What I Built</h2>
        <p>Datomania is documented as a public-data project around information that should exist in Spain. The rewritten README frames it around the Representantes dataset, 1,257 parliamentarians, provenance modeling, public API/export routes, architecture, methodology, status, and portfolio context.</p>
        <FactsList class="facts">
          <li><strong>Data product</strong><span>Public-interest dataset, browsing surface, methodology, and usability framing.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Provenance</strong><span>Source-aware modeling so records can be inspected rather than blindly trusted.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Developer surface</strong><span>API/export routes make the data useful beyond the UI.</span></li>
        </FactsList>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>System Architecture</h2>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><img src="./assets/datomania-data-product.svg" alt="Datomania civic data product diagram with public sources, provenance model, Representantes records, product surface, API routes, methodology, verification, and evidence needs." loading="lazy" /></div>
          <figcaption>Public-safe product diagram. It captures the data-product shape: public sources, provenance modeling, records, UI, API routes, methodology, and verification.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><img src="./assets/datomania-representantes-home.png" alt="Datomania Representantes dashboard showing 642 parliamentarians, chamber counts, education summary, and a hemicycle visualization." loading="lazy" /></div>
          <figcaption>Local product screenshot from the Representantes dashboard. It shows the civic-data surface, metrics, legislature switcher, and visualization layer.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><img src="./assets/datomania-api-docs.png" alt="Datomania API documentation showing public endpoints, available datasets, base URL, and query parameters." loading="lazy" /></div>
          <figcaption>API documentation screenshot. Datomania exposes the dataset through public endpoints and export routes rather than keeping the data trapped in the UI.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><img src="./assets/datomania-live-site.png" alt="Live Datomania homepage showing the DATOMANIA title, open-source status, auditable code, JSON CSV API data, MIT license, and GitHub link." loading="lazy" /></div>
          <figcaption>Live-site screenshot from <code>https://datomania.info</code>. It proves the public product is reachable, open-source positioned, and linked to inspectable code and data surfaces.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>Technical Decisions</h2>
        <PointsList class="points">
          <li>Frame the project around public usefulness instead of only data collection.</li>
          <li>Make provenance and methodology part of the product surface.</li>
          <li>Expose API/export routes so the dataset can support downstream workflows.</li>
          <li>Keep the README explicit about architecture and verification, not just a product description.</li>
        </PointsList>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>What This Proves</h2>
        <p>Datomania shows product judgment in a less glamorous but highly practical domain: turning messy public information into a browsable, inspectable, reusable data product with clear provenance and engineering discipline.</p>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>Public Evidence</h2>
        <PointsList class="points">
          <li>Public repo: <code>gorkamolero/datomania</code>.</li>
          <li>Live public site: <code>https://datomania.info</code>.</li>
          <li>README rewritten and pushed.</li>
          <li><code>pnpm lint</code>, <code>pnpm test:run</code>, and <code>pnpm build</code> passed.</li>
          <li>Product, table, API-doc, and live public-site screenshots captured.</li>
          <li>Stats/export proof — available on request.</li>
        </PointsList>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>Review Boundary</h2>
        <p>Confirm source terms, methodology notes, and exported fields before using live-site screenshots in public application materials.</p>
        <ActionRow class="actions"><TextLink class="button primary" href="https://datomania.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open live site</TextLink>
          <TextLink class="button primary" href="https://github.com/gorkamolero/datomania" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open repo</TextLink></ActionRow>
      </WorkSection>
      </main>
  </PageFrame>
  <Fragment slot="after-footer" set:html={afterFooter} />
</Base>
